    "text": "Gaul was an ancient Celtic land. It covers lands now part of France. It also included areas of modern Belgium, Germany, and Switzerland. Julius Caesar brought these lands under Roman power. He wrote about them in his Gallic Wars. Much of what we know about continental Celts comes from Caesar. His truthfulness is hard to gauge. He wanted political power over the Celts. The Gauls were not one tribe. They were many tribal peoples. They shared a common language and roughly common beliefs and customs.",
